From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baraneedharan Anbazhagan <anbazhagan@hp.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:43:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg: Fix OptionOrder double free

Remove the duplicate OptionOrder free on reallocation failure in
EfiBootManagerGetLoadOptions().

Signed-off-by: Anbazhagan Baraneedharan <anbazhagan@hp.com>

ouroBIOS backport of tianocore/edk2 commit 011eca2e8f8b (merged on
2026-11-03, after edk2-stable202608, the base of MrChromebox's
uefipayload_2608), applied unchanged. Drop it when the base includes
it.

Why here: BdsDxe reads the load options with
EfiBootManagerGetLoadOptions() at every boot. When a ####Order variable
names options that do not exist and shrinking the array then failed,
it freed OptionOrder a second time; only when the memory is exhausted.

TEST=git am on the series: clean, the same lines as upstream.
---
 MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmLoadOption.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmLoadOption.c b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmLoadOption.c
index 66faf5732..1499f908b 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmLoadOption.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmLoadOption.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 Copyright (c) 2011 - 2019, Intel Corporation. All rights reserved.<BR>
 (C) Copyright 2015-2018 Hewlett Packard Enterprise Development LP<BR>
+(c) Copyright 2026 HP Development Company, L.P.
 SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
 
 **/
@@ -1163,7 +1164,6 @@ EfiBootManagerGetLoadOptions (
       Options = ReallocatePool (*OptionCount * sizeof (EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION), OptionIndex * sizeof (EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION), Options);
       if (Options == NULL) {
         ASSERT (Options != NULL);
-        FreePool (OptionOrder);
         return NULL;
       }
 
